from audit_helpers import *
reasons={816:'The split torus in the scan has subscript m, G_m^I. Restore the misplaced plus sign to a subscript.',817:'The print has the nonword indénée. The intended indexing of the character family is indexée; retain the nonword only diplomatically.',818:'The quotient visibly uses V_0 with a subscript, not V minus zero.',819:'The scan writes Gal(bar F/F), although F already denotes the algebraic closure and the coinvariants are taken under arithmetic Frobenius over F_q. Correct to Gal(F/F_q).',820:'The proof visibly asks for an embedding k into F_q, impossible for a general extension of degree N. The preceding lemma states the intended embedding into F; remove subscript q in corrected forms.',821:'The right side of the isomorphism visibly uses the finite-field/algebraic-closure double-struck F, not plain italic F.',822:'The printed phrase is opérateur de permutation circulaire, singular.',823:'Parentheses around the product are visible in the scan and indicate the tuple of coordinates indexed by i. Restore them.',824:'The proposition says à coefficient dans, singular; preserve the printed formulation.',825:'The scan says Les points ... résultent donc, not résultant.',826:'The print says une famille de caractère, singular. The indexed family consists of characters, so the plural s is needed.',827:'The opening formula visibly names K_n with subscript n. Restore the omitted index.',828:'The trace subscript is reversed in print as F_q/k. The algebra k is finite étale over F_q, so the trace has source k and target F_q.',829:'The scan names Cycle 1.3 example 2. The prefix VI in Miller points to the wrong chapter; restore the Cycle chapter IV target.',830:'The final factor is visibly F(psi), but this is the multiplicative-character pullback N*F(chi); each coordinate factor must be F(chi).',831:'The scan uses a multiplication dot between chi^{-1} composed with N and psi composed with trace. Restore the product instead of a comma.',832:'The cardinal is printed as lowercase n, but the degree of k and cardinality of I are N, distinct from the Kummer exponent n. Correct this reference to N.',833:'The left side of (4.12.1) visibly has V without its star. The character sheaf lives on the unit torus V*, as in both surrounding formulas; supply the star in corrected forms.',834:'The right side of (4.12.1) lacks the N-fold tensor power on H_c^1. The preceding Künneth formula and the following Frobenius trace to the Nth power both require it.'}
for n,reason in reasons.items():decide(n,reason)
